; Fleet clj-kondo config — copied byte-identical to
; .clj-kondo/config.edn in each adopted repo (see cljfmt.edn header
; for the sync law). v1 pins the tool floor and otherwise runs the
; clj-kondo DEFAULT linter levels: the Phase 1 census measures the
; default gate. Linter levels are never demoted to make a repo pass;
; off-by-default idiom linters are enabled in deliberate fleet-wide
; batches, recorded here.
{:min-clj-kondo-version "2026.10.26"
 ;; ── eve.db.ds repo exception (sync-law named exception, see STATUS) ──
 ;; Eve ships no clj-kondo exports, so kondo cannot see that
 ;; eve.alpha/deftype (used as `eve/deftype`) and eve.deftype/deftype
 ;; are structurally clojure.core/deftype: a name, a field vector,
 ;; then protocol specs whose bodies close over the fields. Without
 ;; this mapping every field reference reads as an unresolved symbol
 ;; and every protocol method as an invalid arity. Same exception as
 ;; narcis (Phase 1 RETRO item 1); proposed upstream homes: Eve ships
 ;; clj-kondo exports for its macros, or the fleet template gains
 ;; this mapping for Eve-consuming repos.
 :lint-as {clojure.pprint/print-length-loop clojure.core/loop
           eve.alpha/deftype clojure.core/deftype
           eve.deftype/deftype clojure.core/deftype}
 ;; ── symbol-exact exclusion, same shape as the Eve lane's ──
 ;; thrown-msg? is a clojure.test/cljs.test assert-expr DISPATCH
 ;; symbol (defmethod t/assert-expr 'thrown-msg? at
 ;; test/eve/db/ds/test_macros.clj:22 and the supports' :clj arms):
 ;; it appears only as the head symbol of (is (thrown-msg? ...))
 ;; forms and is never a var. Proven at recount2 (all 23 sites are
 ;; inside `is` forms). Symbol-exact: any other unresolved symbol
 ;; still errors.
 :linters {:unresolved-symbol {:exclude [thrown-msg?]}}
 ;; redefined-var is NOT excluded here — kondo 2026.10.26 does
 ;; not honor :exclude for that linter (measured). The 21
 ;; cljs-stub-idiom sites in eve.db.ds.db carry per-site ignores
 ;; with reasons instead.
 ;; ── this repo's own defining macros, taught by analyze-call hooks
 ;; (.clj-kondo/hooks/eve_db_ds.cljc): parser/deftrecord (record
 ;; types), db/defcomp (comparators), util/cond+ and util/if+
 ;; (cond with :let clauses). Same-ns macros are not reached by
 ;; :lint-as (measured in the Phase 2 lane: lint-as on a same-ns
 ;; macro is ignored), so hooks carry these.
 :hooks {:analyze-call {eve.db.ds.parser/deftrecord hooks.eve-db-ds/deftrecord
                        eve.db.ds.db/defcomp hooks.eve-db-ds/defcomp
                        eve.db.ds.util/cond+ hooks.eve-db-ds/cond+
                        eve.db.ds.util/if+ hooks.eve-db-ds/if+
                        eve.db.ds.db/defn+ hooks.eve-db-ds/defn+
                        eve.db.ds.db/defrecord-updatable hooks.eve-db-ds/defrecord-updatable
                        eve.db.ds.core/sci-fn hooks.eve-db-ds/sci-fn
                        eve.db.ds.core/db-fn hooks.eve-db-ds/db-fn
                        ;; Eve deftype needs the Eve lane's analyze-call
                        ;; hook (.clj-kondo/hooks/eve_deftype.clj, copied
                        ;; from SeniorCareMarket/eve's Phase 2 lane —
                        ;; the same hook Eve ships in its kondo export):
                        ;; :lint-as to clojure.core/deftype cannot model
                        ;; Eve deftype's #?@ protocol-group vectors or
                        ;; per-pass protocol translation, and reads the
                        ;; Datom/DB/FilteredDB bodies as hundreds of
                        ;; unresolved symbols + unused bindings (measured
                        ;; at recount2: db.cljc alone carried 190
                        ;; findings, nearly all inside eve/deftype forms).
                        eve.alpha/deftype hooks.eve-deftype/deftype
                        eve.deftype/deftype hooks.eve-deftype/deftype}}}
